  <Patch Id="P2KZXCIndfJSwEfdeiVMIG">
    <Canvas Id="VAgMmzyJldYKuKSc34QL5p" DefaultCategory="Main" CanvasType="FullCategory" />
    <Node Name="Application" Bounds="100,100" Id="Pi5RuWhH6PVNiplb8lVns8">
      <p:NodeReference>
        <Choice Kind="ContainerDefinition" Name="Process" />
        <FullNameCategoryReference ID="Primitive" />
      </p:NodeReference>
      <Patch Id="VP6Eznh52TPIFTVZUiiRwu">
        <Canvas Id="OOvVKziM3ujOp9IVVcSv4b" CanvasType="Group">
          <Pad Id="EBSGVrVqyveLtudRd53hcD" Bounds="-820,-120,620,500" ShowValueBox="true" isIOBox="true" Value="ACT IV LAB - Experiment: the resolution ladder. NOT a shipped unit.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;One place - the summit of Fuji, 138.7274 E 35.3606 N, true height 3776 m - asked its height six&#xD;&#xA;times, once per zoom level 8..13. Six Terrarium tiles, six answers.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;FLIP FETCH ON. Six tiles arrive (about 30-60 KB each, watch the BYTES row). Then read HEIGHT&#xD;&#xA;left to right: it walks toward 3776 as the pixels shrink from ~500 m to ~16 m across. Same&#xD;&#xA;place, same dataset, six different truths - and each one cost one more fetch.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;THE QUESTION THIS PROTOTYPE EXISTS TO ASK: is 'resolution is part of access' a mental-model&#xD;&#xA;shift that keeps recurring? The pyramid under this patch - the same world stored at every zoom,&#xD;&#xA;1/3 extra space so that ANY sharpness is one fetch away - is the same idea as mipmaps, COG&#xD;&#xA;overviews and COPC levels. If the ladder reads as obvious here, the idea may deserve a unit;&#xD;&#xA;if it reads as six numbers, it does not.&#xD;&#xA;&#xD;&#xA;Rules of the lab: no new library surface (every node here shipped already), fetch only on the&#xD;&#xA;toggle, results recorded in docs/ACT-IV-LAB.md. Data: Terrarium terrain tiles (AWS Open Data);&#xD;&#xA;attribution as in Prompt How high is here and THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md.">
            <p:TypeAnnotation LastCategoryFullName="Primitive" LastDependency="VL.CoreLib.vl">
              <Choice Kind="TypeFlag" Name="String" />
            </p:TypeAnnotation>
            <p:ValueBoxSettings>
              <p:fontsize p:Type="Int32">11</p:fontsize>
              <p:stringtype p:Assembly="VL.Core" p:Type="VL.Core.StringType">Comment</p:stringtype>
            </p:ValueBoxSettings>
          </Pad>
          <Pad Id="SKtDI2SrUcxJzBFMq8qYMX" Comment="FETCH" Bounds="60,0,70,35" ShowValueBox="true" isIOBox="true" Value="False">
            <p:TypeAnnotation LastCategoryFullName="Primitive" LastDependency="VL.CoreLib.vl">
              <Choice Kind="TypeFlag" Name="Boolean" />
            </p:TypeAnnotation>
            <p:ValueBoxSettings>
              <p:buttonmode p:Assembly="VL.UI.Forms" p:Type="VL.HDE.PatchEditor.Editors.ButtonModeEnum">Toggle</p:buttonmode>
            </p:ValueBoxSettings>
          </Pad>
          <Pad Id="V2FeXO7o4WJjv4U1n9QtLQ" Bounds="140,0,560,30" ShowValueBox="true" isIOBox="true" Value="&lt;- one toggle, six fetches (one per zoom). Off when you arrive: opening a patch is not agreeing to network traffic - lab or no lab.">
